WEBVTT

00:00.375 --> 00:03.843
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.844 --> 00:07.180
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.181 --> 00:11.017
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.018 --> 00:13.786
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.787 --> 00:17.290
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.291 --> 00:20.726
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:20.727 --> 00:22.295
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.296 --> 00:24.030
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.031 --> 00:29.031
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.478 --> 00:39.946
Ah, the Aiwa Double Tape Deck.

00:39.947 --> 00:42.548
The Waldorf and Statler
of every thrift store.

00:42.549 --> 00:44.083
The selection here stinks.

00:44.084 --> 00:45.650
Yeah, and so do the customers.

00:48.489 --> 00:51.324
Jim Henson died of treatable pneumonia.

00:51.325 --> 00:54.093
<i>Hey, Brian, remember Sisterhood
of the Traveling Pants?</i>

00:54.094 --> 00:56.628
They have the magic girl-power jeans.

00:59.233 --> 01:00.700
Holy crap, what happened?

01:00.701 --> 01:03.669
I don't know. I-I think
I turned into America Ferrera.

01:03.670 --> 01:06.339
I don't want this. Help! Someone, help!

01:06.340 --> 01:08.875
Looking passable, Stewie.

01:08.876 --> 01:11.510
Looking damn passable.

01:13.514 --> 01:17.450
Aw, crap, people we know.
You know the drill.

01:17.451 --> 01:20.386
We're donating, not buying.

01:20.387 --> 01:23.523
Just doing our part to give back
to the community.

01:23.524 --> 01:25.057
I'm gonna go wait in the alley.

01:25.058 --> 01:27.860
Could you just ball them up
and throw them out the window?

01:27.861 --> 01:31.496
Putting on strangers' hats
is always a good idea.

01:37.104 --> 01:38.905
- Thank you for your service.
- Huh?

01:38.906 --> 01:40.473
My father's a veteran, too.

01:40.474 --> 01:42.909
Thank you for protecting us
and for posting revenge porn

01:42.910 --> 01:44.410
on Marine Corps message boards.

01:44.411 --> 01:45.778
Oh, actually, I'm not...

01:45.779 --> 01:47.547
I'm gonna start a trend
of interrupting your sentences.

01:47.548 --> 01:49.115
Well, no, it's just a hat. I didn't...

01:49.116 --> 01:50.249
Thank you for your service.

01:50.250 --> 01:51.717
Bless you and all of our veterans.

01:51.718 --> 01:53.119
No, guys, I-I'm not really a vet...

01:53.120 --> 01:55.154
I don't have time to hear
the rest of your sentence,

01:55.155 --> 01:56.556
but thank you for being a veteran

01:56.557 --> 01:58.324
because you're definitely a veteran.

01:58.325 --> 02:02.228
<i>And I'm Cris Collinsworth
from NBC Sunday Night Football.</i>

02:02.229 --> 02:05.097
On behalf of all TV football dummies,

02:05.098 --> 02:06.899
thank you for your service.

02:06.900 --> 02:09.302
You're-you're welcome.

02:09.303 --> 02:11.671
Wow. Feels real good to be a veteran,

02:11.672 --> 02:14.539
even better than buying
a bottle of Newman's Own.

02:16.143 --> 02:19.244
This makes me a good person.

02:20.647 --> 02:23.482
Hey, someone just bought a
bottle of bland salad dressing.

02:23.483 --> 02:26.818
Now we can use all proceeds
to do jihad stuff.

02:36.063 --> 02:37.730
Hey, Peter, what's with the hat?

02:37.731 --> 02:39.565
- I'm pretending to be a veteran.
- What?

02:39.566 --> 02:42.201
Yeah, it's awesome.
Vets get all the sweet deals.

02:42.202 --> 02:44.170
I mean, you never see a homeless vet.

02:44.171 --> 02:45.605
And people have been really nice.

02:45.606 --> 02:47.572
Everywhere I go, they open doors for me.

02:48.709 --> 02:50.042
Welcome, sir.

02:50.043 --> 02:51.978
Thank you.

02:51.979 --> 02:54.880
<i>Hey, so when really fat people come,</i>

02:54.881 --> 02:57.249
make sure we're opening both doors.

02:57.250 --> 02:59.051
Guys, you could be veterans, too.

02:59.052 --> 03:01.186
Look what happens
when I put on sunglasses.

03:02.556 --> 03:04.156
♪ Highway to the danger zone... ♪

03:04.157 --> 03:06.525
- Wow!
- I want to try.

03:06.526 --> 03:08.561
♪ Highway to the danger zone. ♪

03:08.562 --> 03:10.296
It's loud being a veteran!

03:10.297 --> 03:12.131
The hell is wrong with you guys?!

03:12.132 --> 03:14.400
<i>Do I need to remind you
I actually am a veteran?</i>

03:14.401 --> 03:17.103
And I'm sickened by the thought
of trolling for free handouts

03:17.104 --> 03:19.872
on account of being a vet,
much less pretending to be one.

03:19.873 --> 03:21.674
Quagmire, what if
I told you your glasses

03:21.675 --> 03:23.275
do "Playing With The Boys"?

03:23.276 --> 03:24.644
The volleyball scene?

03:24.645 --> 03:26.379
Go ahead, give it a whirl.

03:26.380 --> 03:28.547
♪ I'm playing... ♪

03:28.548 --> 03:31.751
<i>Whoa! It's like I'm high-fiving
with Anthony Edwards.</i>

03:31.752 --> 03:33.619
<i>And it's not like I'd be lying.</i>

03:33.620 --> 03:36.221
There we go. Hey, another round
for me and my veteran buddies.

03:38.025 --> 03:40.893
<i>Dad, Family Guy used two of your songs.</i>

03:40.894 --> 03:43.229
Well, that's great,
but I'm not your dad.

03:43.230 --> 03:46.332
I'm Kenny Loggins and you're a
groupie I brought here for sex.

03:46.333 --> 03:47.800
<i>Dad, Family Guy just...</i>

03:47.801 --> 03:49.901
<i>See, now, that's my daughter.</i>

03:54.274 --> 03:55.641
You guys got your video cameras ready?

03:55.642 --> 03:57.009
Yeah. What's going on?

03:57.010 --> 04:00.212
Well, as a veteran, I get
to star in a viral YouTube video

04:00.213 --> 04:02.682
of me reuniting with my beloved pet.

04:02.683 --> 04:04.916
So here goes.

04:15.562 --> 04:17.229
My pet is Christian the lion.

04:17.230 --> 04:19.231
I'm doing two Internet things at once.

04:19.232 --> 04:21.233
This is my heterosexual roommate, Ace,

04:21.234 --> 04:23.903
with whom I shared the lion
two decades ago.

04:23.904 --> 04:26.771
- You look great, Peter.
- I have a family now!

04:30.911 --> 04:33.412
You know, guys, if being
a veteran is about anything,

04:33.413 --> 04:35.514
it's about getting half-hearted applause

04:35.515 --> 04:38.017
on a Southwest Airlines flight.

04:38.018 --> 04:39.418
Veterans.

04:39.419 --> 04:41.487
Yay, veterans.

04:41.488 --> 04:44.590
<i>Holy crap, you're Eric Dane
from Marley and Me,</i>

04:44.591 --> 04:46.125
and other stuff!

04:46.126 --> 04:48.394
I'm afraid you got to give us
your front-of-the-plane seats

04:48.395 --> 04:50.463
'cause that's what celebrities
do for veterans.

04:50.464 --> 04:51.630
Well, clear out, kids.

04:51.631 --> 04:53.566
It's just part of the Hollywood deal.

04:53.567 --> 04:55.067
Thank you. Thanks.

04:55.068 --> 04:57.203
Thank you so much. This is why I served.

04:57.204 --> 04:59.238
<i>"USS Nathan James"?</i>

04:59.239 --> 05:01.507
Yes, sir. Boats, military, sir.

05:01.508 --> 05:03.542
<i>The Nathan James is the fictitious ship</i>

05:03.543 --> 05:07.847
<i>on TNT's The Last Ship, starring
Adam Baldwin and Jocko Sims.</i>

05:07.848 --> 05:10.216
- And Eric Dane.
- Uh-oh.

05:10.217 --> 05:12.584
You guys aren't veterans at all.
You're frauds.

05:13.920 --> 05:15.755
Okay, we ain't real vets.

05:15.756 --> 05:17.456
Quagmire served in the Navy.

05:17.457 --> 05:19.892
The rest of us are charlatans.

05:19.893 --> 05:21.427
- Boo!
- You're terrible!

05:21.428 --> 05:25.331
I fly Southwest to have a classy
experience and you've ruined it.

05:25.332 --> 05:28.167
Excuse me, gentlemen.
You're under arrest.

05:28.168 --> 05:29.435
What?! Why?!

05:29.436 --> 05:31.771
You three are in violation
of the Stolen Valor Act,

05:31.772 --> 05:34.240
which makes it a crime
to pretend to be a veteran.

05:34.241 --> 05:36.776
Oh, so suddenly it's a crime
to break the law?

05:36.777 --> 05:38.577
Mr. Quagmire, you're free to go,

05:38.578 --> 05:40.613
but the rest of you
will have to come with me.

05:40.614 --> 05:42.114
I thought we had it bad,

05:42.115 --> 05:43.449
being gay overhead bins.

05:43.450 --> 05:44.784
What makes us gay?

05:44.785 --> 05:46.184
We've got bags in our mouths.

05:52.893 --> 05:54.426
Hey, quick, put these on.

05:54.427 --> 05:56.428
They're not gonna throw
a veteran in jail.

05:56.429 --> 05:58.130
Is this some kind of joke to you?

05:58.131 --> 05:59.632
No, it was a sincere idea.

05:59.633 --> 06:01.233
Real servicemen and women

06:01.234 --> 06:03.803
have made real sacrifices
for this country.

06:03.804 --> 06:06.505
And you. You're an actual
veteran; you should know better.

06:06.506 --> 06:07.873
I'm sorry.

06:07.874 --> 06:09.942
You made a mockery
of our whole family, Glenn.

06:09.943 --> 06:11.477
Now, everywhere I go,

06:11.478 --> 06:14.113
it's like people are staring
at me and whispering.

06:14.114 --> 06:15.581
Court is now in session.

06:15.582 --> 06:18.184
Judge Dignified Q. Blackman presiding.

06:18.185 --> 06:21.353
You men are accused of violating
the Stolen Valor Act,

06:21.354 --> 06:23.589
and that's years of jail time.

06:23.590 --> 06:25.191
We forgot to get a lawyer.

06:25.192 --> 06:27.660
But in view of your long service
to comedy,

06:27.661 --> 06:29.728
I'm willing to offer a deal.

06:29.729 --> 06:31.030
What kind of deal?

06:31.031 --> 06:34.166
I'll waive the charges,
but only on the condition

06:34.167 --> 06:36.769
that you men enlist
in the military for real.

06:36.770 --> 06:39.672
You three have to join the Marines.

06:39.673 --> 06:42.675
Oh, my God. We could be killed!
Please, no!

06:42.676 --> 06:44.310
All right, how about the Coast Guard?

06:44.311 --> 06:45.878
Yeah, that's fine.

06:45.879 --> 06:47.079
- Wow.
- Something happened.

06:47.080 --> 06:48.480
Something just happened in court.

06:48.481 --> 06:51.050
Glenn, if you were half the man
I used to be,

06:51.051 --> 06:53.819
you'd stand up and join them.

06:53.820 --> 06:55.821
Your Honor? I'd like to sign up, too.

06:55.822 --> 06:57.089
Oh, my God.

06:57.090 --> 06:58.490
I was checking my phone. What happened?

06:58.491 --> 06:59.658
Excuse me?

06:59.659 --> 07:00.926
That's right. I'm going with them.

07:00.927 --> 07:03.762
The four of us will join
the Coast Guard together.

07:03.763 --> 07:06.565
All right. Report to
the induction center tomorrow.

07:06.566 --> 07:08.767
Court is adjourned.

07:08.768 --> 07:12.304
<i>The People v. Ted 2.</i>

07:12.305 --> 07:14.172
Okay, come on, let's get out
of here. Let's go. Let's go.

07:18.710 --> 07:20.644
Good morning, recruits.

07:20.645 --> 07:22.212
Welcome to the Coast Guard.

07:22.213 --> 07:24.648
Sir, when do we report
for basic training, sir?

07:24.649 --> 07:26.550
Hey, what's with the "sir" stuff?

07:26.551 --> 07:28.251
This is just the Coast Guard.

07:28.252 --> 07:31.021
Now, come on. Who here can
pantomime driving a boat?

07:31.022 --> 07:33.456
Hmm, we got any boat guys here?

07:35.560 --> 07:36.860
Whoa, look at that.

07:36.861 --> 07:38.762
You guys should be recruiting me.

07:38.763 --> 07:41.163
Now can you bounce
with the waves a little bit?

07:43.134 --> 07:45.736
Uh-oh! Getting kind of choppy.

07:45.737 --> 07:47.771
Is this guy for real? This is idiotic.

07:47.772 --> 07:49.606
This is nothing like what the Navy was.

07:49.607 --> 07:51.875
Shh, Quagmire, I got to focus
on my boat here.

07:51.876 --> 07:53.910
The way people's talking makes me think

07:53.911 --> 07:57.013
we're gonna be dealing
with a lot of water.

07:57.014 --> 07:58.715
You guys seem to have what it takes,

07:58.716 --> 08:01.685
so raise your right hand as
I recite the Coast Guard pledge.

08:01.686 --> 08:03.954
"When you're here, you're family."

08:03.955 --> 08:06.555
- Isn't that the slogan for...?
- We had it first!

08:07.725 --> 08:09.526
Everybody ships out tomorrow.

08:09.527 --> 08:11.962
You'll find your assignments
listed on this sheet.

08:11.963 --> 08:16.533
Oh, crap. Where in Iraq
is "Fort El Ahoud Urd Ali"?

08:16.534 --> 08:18.034
Peter, that's Fort Lauderdale.

08:18.035 --> 08:21.104
We're being shipped out to guard
freakin' spring break.

08:21.105 --> 08:22.439
- Sweet!
- All right!

08:22.440 --> 08:24.207
Spring break on the land, not the water!

08:24.208 --> 08:27.077
No, it's not sweet. It's a joke.
This whole thing is a joke!

08:27.078 --> 08:29.279
Compared to the Navy,
the Coast Guard is totally

08:29.280 --> 08:32.883
unprofessional and incompetent,
like that ancient Roman intern.

08:32.884 --> 08:35.986
This is Markus. Today's his first day.

08:35.987 --> 08:40.557
He's going to be crucifying you now.

08:40.558 --> 08:43.693
He might want to use his hammer.

08:43.694 --> 08:45.796
Ugh, sorry. I'm so bad at this.

08:45.797 --> 08:48.497
Relax, you're doing fine.

08:52.270 --> 08:53.837
Well, I'm off.

08:53.838 --> 08:55.806
Oh, Peter, I'm so worried.

08:55.807 --> 08:58.175
- Where are they stationing you?
- I can't tell you.

08:58.176 --> 09:00.376
That is on a knead-the-dough basis.

09:03.047 --> 09:04.481
- Florida?!
- Shh!

09:04.482 --> 09:06.817
Hey, you be safe.

09:06.818 --> 09:10.687
Wait, Dad, before you go,
can you teach me to shave?

09:10.688 --> 09:13.223
Well, for starters, bud, that's
supposed to be on your pubes.

09:13.224 --> 09:15.625
You got a secret inch
hiding under there.

09:15.626 --> 09:17.694
This is what I'm gonna be missing.

09:17.695 --> 09:20.230
Well, that's an unrelated car honking,

09:20.231 --> 09:21.931
but I'm gonna go now.

09:30.141 --> 09:32.809
Fort Lauderdale, Florida,

09:32.810 --> 09:36.413
where all the art in every
dentist's office comes from.

09:36.414 --> 09:38.582
All right, let's get to work.
Grab your binoculars.

09:38.583 --> 09:40.317
We got to practice
doing funny double-takes

09:40.318 --> 09:41.951
upon seeing a bikini woman.

09:47.124 --> 09:49.192
Sir, should I say, "Aaoogah," sir?

09:49.193 --> 09:51.828
Affirmative. And, Joe, I order
you to just let the binoculars

09:51.829 --> 09:54.297
fall right out of your hands,
but you don't even notice

09:54.298 --> 09:56.032
'cause of how foxy the woman is.

09:56.033 --> 09:57.467
All right, yeah.

09:57.468 --> 10:00.003
I can see that we got the right
skill set for this assignment.

10:00.004 --> 10:01.438
Okay, guys, knock it off.

10:01.439 --> 10:04.441
But, Quagmire, there's
spring break boobs everywhere!

10:04.442 --> 10:05.742
Come on, guys, I mean it.

10:05.743 --> 10:08.578
This is important. I want you
to start acting like it.

10:08.579 --> 10:10.413
- Wow, he's serious.
- He's very serious.

10:10.414 --> 10:12.214
We're in the motel now.

10:16.487 --> 10:19.189
Guys, we have to complete
a 160-point inspection

10:19.190 --> 10:20.657
of this coastal patrol cutter.

10:20.658 --> 10:21.825
I'll call them out.

10:21.826 --> 10:24.928
Item one: Hydraulic grapple-winch.

10:24.929 --> 10:26.296
Guys?

10:26.297 --> 10:28.864
We're over here,
painting clever names on boats.

10:38.609 --> 10:41.678
No, Peter, it's supposed
to be short and poppy.

10:41.679 --> 10:43.679
Oh, okay.

10:50.488 --> 10:53.790
Okay, guys, while I scan
for disabled watercraft,

10:53.791 --> 10:56.693
I need a status report
on that hydraulic grapple-winch.

10:56.694 --> 10:58.061
Guys?

10:58.062 --> 11:00.230
We're busy;
we're hanging out with Aquaman.

11:00.231 --> 11:01.998
I told you, I'm not Aquaman.

11:01.999 --> 11:03.533
I am the Sub-Mariner.

11:03.534 --> 11:05.669
- What's your deal?
- I'm just like Aquaman,

11:05.670 --> 11:07.537
but I can't get fish to do things.

11:07.538 --> 11:08.838
That's the big thing.

11:08.839 --> 11:10.807
I mean, isn't that all Aquaman does?

11:10.808 --> 11:12.742
No, he can also breathe underwater,

11:12.743 --> 11:14.444
and he's strong, like me.

11:14.445 --> 11:16.313
Isn't everyone strong underwater?

11:16.314 --> 11:18.148
No, no. Not like me.

11:18.149 --> 11:21.351
I can punch a big octopus
a really long way.

11:21.352 --> 11:22.519
Hey, guys.

11:22.520 --> 11:24.187
- Hey, Aquaman!
- Yeah!

11:24.188 --> 11:26.089
Hey, make a fish do something.

11:26.090 --> 11:27.991
Aw, shucks, guys, I don't know.

11:27.992 --> 11:30.659
I guess I could do
something like... this.

11:35.866 --> 11:38.134
Wow, a real superhero.

11:38.135 --> 11:40.971
I-I have little wings on my feet!

11:40.972 --> 11:43.306
No, just-just, shh, shh.
Ju... it's over.

11:43.307 --> 11:44.773
It's over.

11:49.680 --> 11:51.314
Hey, can you guys
keep it down for a bit?

11:51.315 --> 11:53.350
I got to have a FaceTime
conversation with my wife

11:53.351 --> 11:55.418
where we talk at the same time,
and then stop,

11:55.419 --> 11:56.919
and then start again, then laugh.

12:00.091 --> 12:01.257
- Hi, hon...
- Hi, hon...

12:01.258 --> 12:02.592
- No, no, you go...
- You go ahead.

12:02.593 --> 12:04.060
- No, I...
- Go ahead.

12:04.061 --> 12:05.494
- Y-You first.
- You first.

12:07.465 --> 12:09.165
- Hi, Pop.
- Oh, God, Stewie.

12:09.166 --> 12:10.500
You've gotten so big.

12:10.501 --> 12:12.135
No, I'm just in the foreground.

12:12.136 --> 12:13.837
You're as tall as your mother now.

12:13.838 --> 12:15.805
He... he doesn't understand perspective.

12:15.806 --> 12:17.640
All right, let me say good-bye to Mommy.

12:17.641 --> 12:19.676
- Well, you take ca...
- Good-bye, hon...

12:19.677 --> 12:20.777
- You go...
- Oh, what?

12:20.778 --> 12:22.078
- You go...
- No, I was just gonna say...

12:23.581 --> 12:25.315
Everything stinks.

12:25.316 --> 12:27.851
- Hey, Quagmire, where you going?
- I'm going home.

12:27.852 --> 12:29.452
- What? Why?
- 'Cause I'm sick of this.

12:29.453 --> 12:31.187
I'm the only one
taking the job seriously.

12:31.188 --> 12:33.289
Hell, you guys still don't
even know how to operate

12:33.290 --> 12:35.158
a simple hydraulic grapple-winch.

12:35.159 --> 12:36.893
Okay, that's the third time
you've mentioned

12:36.894 --> 12:38.361
the hydraulic grapple-winch.

12:38.362 --> 12:40.130
Is that gonna be important for later?

12:40.131 --> 12:42.198
I feel like maybe it is.

12:42.199 --> 12:43.700
Quagmire, you can't just go home.

12:43.701 --> 12:45.001
We're stationed here.

12:45.002 --> 12:46.703
I wasn't sentenced, but I came anyway

12:46.704 --> 12:49.005
because I thought I could try
and teach my friends

12:49.006 --> 12:51.474
what it means to serve
their country, the way I did.

12:51.475 --> 12:54.744
But you're hopeless, so I'm done.

12:54.745 --> 12:56.546
And I'm still the voice

12:56.547 --> 12:59.081
of Cris Collinsworth, and I'm done, too.

13:00.484 --> 13:02.419
Uhp, closet.

13:02.420 --> 13:04.320
Now I got it.

13:04.321 --> 13:05.755
Aw.

13:05.756 --> 13:08.658
I disappointed the stupidest guy
in football.

13:08.659 --> 13:11.561
- I got to go take a sad pee.
- Me, too.

13:11.562 --> 13:14.297
We should probably all go
urinate together, outdoors,

13:14.298 --> 13:17.700
as a group of guys, while
wearing backwards baseball caps,

13:17.701 --> 13:20.836
per Fort Lauderdale municipal law.

13:22.373 --> 13:24.374
The Florida ways are the best ways.

13:24.375 --> 13:26.109
Are we ready to attack?

13:26.110 --> 13:29.279
We are! And many people will die.

13:29.280 --> 13:30.580
What the hell's that?

13:35.219 --> 13:36.820
Are we ready to attack?

13:36.821 --> 13:40.223
We are! And many people will die.

13:40.224 --> 13:42.225
- Oh, my God.
- Those evil frat boys

13:42.226 --> 13:44.327
are planning to kill spring break.

13:44.328 --> 13:47.230
And they only had time to record
two lines of dialogue.

13:47.231 --> 13:48.798
Are we ready to attack?

13:48.799 --> 13:52.034
We are! And many people will die.

13:55.973 --> 13:58.074
- We got to stop them.
- All right, let's just find

13:58.075 --> 14:00.110
a quiet place to come up with a plan.

14:00.111 --> 14:01.744
All right, here's what we do!

14:01.745 --> 14:04.080
We track down...

14:04.081 --> 14:06.416
we saw talking and...

14:06.417 --> 14:08.918
Joe, you get us some...

14:08.919 --> 14:11.387
And, Cleveland, I want you to get...

14:11.388 --> 14:13.957
buildings in the city.

14:13.958 --> 14:17.060
I'm still very unclear about the plan!

14:17.061 --> 14:19.062
Three more banana daiquiris.

14:19.063 --> 14:21.330
We track down the...

14:26.364 --> 14:28.432
Did you see all
of those guns and weapons

14:28.433 --> 14:30.034
those evil frat boys had?

14:30.035 --> 14:31.502
I sure did.

14:31.503 --> 14:34.271
And we still haven't nailed down
a date for visiting Epcot.

14:34.272 --> 14:35.473
But what can we do?

14:35.474 --> 14:38.209
Quagmire was the only
real soldier among us.

14:38.210 --> 14:39.844
You're right. Compared to him,

14:39.845 --> 14:43.246
we're about as useless as one of
those automatic bathroom sinks.

14:47.185 --> 14:49.185
Uhp. Uhp.

14:51.590 --> 14:53.256
Uhp.

14:55.260 --> 14:58.095
Uhp.

14:58.096 --> 14:59.663
Uhp. Uhp.

14:59.664 --> 15:01.065
Uhp. Uhp. Uhp.

15:01.066 --> 15:02.132
Uhp.

15:02.133 --> 15:03.601
Uhp. Uhp.

15:03.602 --> 15:06.203
What the hell are you doing?
This is a women's bathroom.

15:06.204 --> 15:07.805
Uhp.

15:07.806 --> 15:10.741
Come on, guys, we don't need
Quagmire to do the right thing.

15:10.742 --> 15:11.976
I love that movie.

15:11.977 --> 15:13.978
If there's gonna be an attack
at spring break,

15:13.979 --> 15:18.415
we can't just stand by while
people get hurt, or even killed.

15:18.416 --> 15:21.185
Joe's right. It's up to us to stop it.

15:21.186 --> 15:23.020
Because we're in the Coast Guard,

15:23.021 --> 15:25.788
and when you're here, you're family.

15:40.872 --> 15:42.039
- Great!
- Yeah!

15:42.040 --> 15:45.109
- Ooh!
- Yeah, yeah.

15:45.110 --> 15:47.710
That food was all very salty.

15:51.750 --> 15:53.517
There's so many people.

15:53.518 --> 15:56.119
We got to find those frat boys.
Look for anything suspicious.

15:57.255 --> 15:59.790
The Coors party ball is a dirty bomb!

15:59.791 --> 16:02.826
No, Peter, it's not; it's just
the coolest, freshest way

16:02.827 --> 16:05.195
to keep your party rolling
is what it is.

16:05.196 --> 16:06.463
This is hopeless!

16:06.464 --> 16:08.599
There's no way
to guess what their target is.

16:08.600 --> 16:10.234
Final boarding call

16:10.235 --> 16:12.069
for the "Are We Ready To Attack, We Are,

16:12.070 --> 16:14.204
And Many People Will Die" booze cruise.

16:14.205 --> 16:16.640
Okay, I got a feeling about that one.

16:16.641 --> 16:18.375
- Let's go!
- No, guys.

16:18.376 --> 16:19.977
We'll never make it on foot.

16:19.978 --> 16:21.979
We got to steal that kid's Jet Ski.

16:21.980 --> 16:24.582
Peter, the boat's right there.
We'll totally make it.

16:24.583 --> 16:26.082
It's the only way, guys!

16:27.719 --> 16:30.054
Peter, we're now literally
standing on the boat.

16:30.055 --> 16:31.888
That's how close the boat is.

16:32.958 --> 16:34.525
Made it!

16:34.526 --> 16:37.226
- You wanted to ride the Jet Ski.
- I wanted to ride the Jet Ski.

16:41.266 --> 16:43.934
How much you reckon
a boat like this cost?

16:43.935 --> 16:47.137
All right, everybody, freeze!
This is the U.S. Coast Guard.

16:47.138 --> 16:49.405
And when you're here, you're family.

17:03.288 --> 17:06.389
Anyway, U.S. Coast Guard.
You kids are...

17:07.959 --> 17:10.427
What are we gonna do?
We're way outgunned.

17:10.428 --> 17:11.862
Are any of you familiar

17:11.863 --> 17:14.598
with what's referred to
as a "Leeroy Jenkins"?

17:14.599 --> 17:16.233
Well, I don't know what that is,

17:16.234 --> 17:18.535
but let's make a very long,
elaborate plan.

17:18.536 --> 17:21.271
All right, so I'll run in first
and use an intimidating shout.

17:21.272 --> 17:22.473
When my shout's done,

17:22.474 --> 17:24.608
I'll need Joe to come in
and use his shout, too.

17:24.609 --> 17:25.776
What do you think, Joe?

17:25.777 --> 17:27.277
Can you give me
a number crunch real quick?

17:27.278 --> 17:29.213
Yeah, give me a sec.
I'm coming up with, uh,

17:29.214 --> 17:31.949
32.33, repeating, of course.

17:31.950 --> 17:33.851
Okay, that's a lot better
than we usually do.

17:33.852 --> 17:37.221
- So let's...
- Leeroy Jenkins!

17:37.222 --> 17:39.890
Oh, my God, he just ran in.
Let's go! Stick to the plan!

17:39.891 --> 17:41.325
Let's go, let's go!

17:41.326 --> 17:43.794
Aw, man.

17:43.795 --> 17:44.962
Aw, we're dying.

17:44.963 --> 17:46.797
Damn it, Cleveland.

17:46.798 --> 17:48.232
Where'd they get dragons?

17:48.233 --> 17:50.768
These guys have magic, guys.

17:50.769 --> 17:52.169
I can't move.

17:52.170 --> 17:54.571
Oh, God!

17:54.572 --> 17:56.740
You know, Cleveland, you're an idiot.

17:56.741 --> 18:00.443
This episode has
a lot of Internet things.

18:03.415 --> 18:05.416
Ah, crap, we're gonna die.

18:05.417 --> 18:06.717
Freeze!

18:08.353 --> 18:10.187
Quagmire, you came back!

18:10.188 --> 18:12.589
That's right. Because I'm in
the U.S. Coast Guard.

18:12.590 --> 18:14.657
- And when you're here...
- Oh, no, don't say it!

18:21.232 --> 18:23.567
Ah, I'm glad you came back, buddy.

18:23.568 --> 18:24.935
You really saved the day.

18:24.936 --> 18:26.737
Hey, where'd you get the machine gun?

18:26.738 --> 18:28.539
From the coastal patrol cutter.

18:28.540 --> 18:32.443
"Machine gun" is item 49
of the 160-point inspection.

18:32.444 --> 18:35.746
Oh, that was when I was writing
homosexual stuff on the boat.

18:35.747 --> 18:38.115
- Too bad about the bomb.
- Bomb?

18:38.116 --> 18:39.850
Yep. Right here on the boat.

18:39.851 --> 18:42.853
Soon you will all do
the foamy dance of death.

18:42.854 --> 18:46.390
We are! And many people will die.

18:46.391 --> 18:48.424
He just says that one thing.

18:53.631 --> 18:56.466
The bomb is hidden in the foam.

19:01.306 --> 19:02.306
Where is it?

19:02.307 --> 19:03.907
- Have you found it?
- No.

19:03.908 --> 19:06.610
I was thinking next Thursday
for Epcot, but no bomb.

19:06.611 --> 19:09.146
You're wasting your time;
the bomb will activate

19:09.147 --> 19:10.948
the moment the floor stops vibrating.

19:10.949 --> 19:13.317
Did you hear that? Twerk!

19:13.318 --> 19:15.052
Twerk like you're Miley Cyrus

19:15.053 --> 19:17.053
trying to prove something to your dad!

19:25.230 --> 19:26.530
Found it!

19:30.401 --> 19:32.236
We're all gonna die!

19:32.237 --> 19:35.938
Oh, no, we're not.
I stole a Jet Ski from a kid.

19:44.616 --> 19:46.549
Ha, ha!

19:48.987 --> 19:50.553
Oh, I forgot they do that.

19:53.591 --> 19:55.626
Hydraulic grapple-winch!

19:55.627 --> 19:58.094
- Oh, yeah!
- From earlier!

20:12.010 --> 20:14.945
- We did it! It's over.
- 'Cause of you.

20:14.946 --> 20:16.947
Thanks for saving us, Quagmire.

20:16.948 --> 20:19.817
Eh, I was just doing my duty.
Just like you did.

20:19.818 --> 20:21.552
Good job, soldier.

20:21.553 --> 20:24.855
Anyway, what matters is everyone's okay,

20:24.856 --> 20:26.523
thanks to the Coast Guard.

20:26.524 --> 20:28.524
Because when you're here...

20:29.861 --> 20:32.628
I'm not going back to that restaurant.

20:32.629 --> 21:33.629
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru